# 1. Authoring System Verification

This document verifies the dynamic authoring capabilities and visual integrity of every content block defined in the r41n architecture specification.

![Sensor Node Pipeline](/images/architecture.svg)

{% warning title="Operational Risk" %}
Executing unauthorized intrusion telemetry on production environments without formal rules of engagement violates legal standards.
{% /warning %}

The pipeline processes event sequences by hooking Linux syscall boundaries using unprivileged tracepoints or kernel modules depending on privilege level.

```bash
# Verify auditd and eBPF collection status
systemctl status r41n-sensor.service --no-pager
auditctl -l
```

{% note title="Architecture Note" %}
The sensor engine runs entirely in user-space utilizing libbpf ring buffers to prevent kernel panics during high IOPS workloads.
{% /note %}

{% terminal title="sensor-health" commands=[{"cmd":"r41n-sensor --health-check","output":"[+] Sensor Daemon: ACTIVE\n[+] Ring Buffer: 64MB allocated (0.4% utilized)\n[+] Dropped Events: 0\n[*] Status: NOMINAL"}] /%}

![Sensor Node Secondary Pipeline](/images/architecture.svg)

## 2. Advanced Adversary Simulation Lab

{% lab target="10.10.110.45" environment="Debian 12 Target Host" %}
Objective: Enumerate stealth persistence mechanisms placed within systemd generator directories and restore host integrity.
{% /lab %}

{% finding severity="high" cvss="7.8" %}
Arbitrary unit file write permissions identified in `/etc/systemd/system/multi-user.target.wants/`. An unprivileged local operator could escalate privileges by manipulating ExecStart directives.
{% /finding %}

{% mitigation status="Remediated" %}
Restricted write permissions to `root:root` with strict `0644` umask and applied immutable ext4 flags on critical target directories.
{% /mitigation %}

